run - load and execute an ELF program

Description:
The 'run' command loads a user ELF executable from the file system and
transfers control to it through the kernel loader. Use it to run programs
compiled with baoc or other ELF binaries that are not installed as shell
commands under /programs.

Usage:
run <program> [args...]

Examples:
run /programs/out1
run /programs/out1 -code
run /programs/myprog arg1 arg2

Notes:
Programs under /programs or /programs/utils can also be started directly
by name from the shell (e.g. 'calc'). Use 'run' for arbitrary paths,
especially baoc output files.
